WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:09.367
In this walkthrough we'll find and
inspect the instruments that trades are
booked against, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:22.100
Instruments are registered separately from trades. The
bond used in the earlier walkthrough existed here first,
which is why it could be found by its ISIN during deal capture.

3
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:32.633
The register lists what the system can
trade — type, name, currency, maturity
and status, with the identifier alongside.

4
00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:42.367
Search finds an instrument by name or
identifier, which is the quickest route
when you already know what you are looking for.

5
00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:51.767
The type filter narrows it a different
way, to bonds or futures contracts,
when you are browsing rather than searching.

6
00:00:51.767 --> 00:01:02.200
Expanding a row shows the full
definition — the terms that make the
instrument what it is, and which valuations depend on.

7
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:15.900
Deactivate rather than delete is the pattern here. An
instrument that trades already point at cannot be removed
outright, so it is retired instead and stops appearing in pickers.

8
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:25.600
That completes Managing Instruments. Every surface
shown here can also be opened from the agent panel
on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
